   "gap": "Wald's second identity (thm:p15-os-wald-second, handbook/parts/p15/optional-stopping-and-random-walks.tex lines 170-179) asserts S_{T and n} -> S_T in L2 and E S_T^2 = sigma^2 E T for any T with E T < infinity without stating that T is a stopping time. The held source's Exercise 4.8.4 (Durrett v5, printed p. 261 = PDF p. 269) states 'if T is a stopping time with ET < infinity'. The annex proof (handbook/annex/p15/optional-stopping-and-random-walks.tex line 186) uses the fact that {T>=j} is F_{j-1}-measurable without the hypothesis being stated. Owed: the entry's statement must carry the stopping-time hypothesis so that the source hypothesis is preserved. The omission is material: with fair signs, T=1 on {xi_1=xi_2} and T=2 otherwise gives E S_T^2 = 1/2 but sigma^2 E T = 3/2. The exit-time lower bound, its strict form and the sigma^2=0 case are present.",
   "blocker": null
  },
